                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Study 1 based on:  McGill D, Van der Vleuten C, Clarke M. Supervisor assessment of clinical and professional competence of medical trainees: a reliability study using workplace data and a focused analytical literature review. Advances in Health Sciences Education 2011;16:405-425. http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10459-011-9296-1\n\nStudy 2:   McGill DA, van der Vleuten CPM, Clarke MJ. A critical evaluation of the validity and the reliability of global competency constructs for supervisor assessment of junior medical trainees. Advances in Health Sciences Education 2013;18:701-725. DOI 10.1007/s10459-012-9410-z\n\nStudy 3: McGill DA, van der Vleuten CPM, Clarke MJ. Construct validation of judgement-based assessments of medical trainees' competency in the workplace using a \"Kanesian\" approach to validation. BMC Medical Education 2015;15:1-11 http://dx.doi.org/10.1186/s12909-015-0520-1\n\nStudy 4: Thesis Chapter 5 Reframing validity evidence as outcome measures for supervisors’ assessment quality: a validity study using confirmatory factor analysis and Generalisability Theory  (under editorial review)\n\nStudy 5: Thesis Chapter 6: Measuring the quality of supervisor assessments: an exploratory validity analysis incorporating statistical process control (under editorial review)"
                }
              }
